// Mirrormere layout (WP-060): greybox blocks (scaled `block_unit`, centered on `pos`). Y is up;
// the ground is 0 m everywhere except the lake basin (terrain.ron). Places, with centers (x, z):
//   Reedwater Landing   ( -72,-128)  boat shed and quay on the south shore (L06)
//   Stillwater Village  (-107, -28)  five houses in knee-deep water; the chief's house at
//                                    (-96, -10) holds Chronicle Page 2; L07 stands on the dry
//                                    east edge at (-76, -34); the belfry shore plug is south of it
//   the backwater       (-145, -28)  a wading pool behind the village, an islet at its middle
//   the Reed Marsh      (-110,  62)  Blight water, reeds, crawlers and stalkers; the road skirts it
//   Ossuary Stair       ( -44, 128)  L08 on the north shore, a sealed crypt mouth behind it
//   the lake            x -60..140, z -120..100: deep water (entities.ron pools); the causeway
//                       (x 80..90, z 30..100) and the ford (z 20..26, 1.6 m under) cross it
//   the Cathedral       island x 60..110, z -20..30: nave x 68..104, z -17..17; forecourt north
//   L09 Cathedral Causeway (85, 56)  on the causeway, 39 m from the nave's fog gate
// Walks between Lanterns are checked by world_state/mirrormere_tests.rs.
(
  landmarks: [
    // --- Borders: 6 m walls on the edge of the world -------------------------------------
    (name: "border_n", kit: "block_unit", pos: (0.0, 3.00, 159.0), scale: (320.0, 6.0, 2.0)),
